    "content": "Somalia's Ministry of Health has placed 10 Somali citizens under quarantine at an Ebola treatment and quarantine facility in Mogadishu after they returned from the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) via Uganda. The measure, announced in a ministry statement on October 12, is a precautionary step to prevent any potential spread of the virus.\n\nThe individuals are currently undergoing laboratory testing and medical follow-up, according to the statement. Health authorities have also begun tracing the people they came into contact with during their journey and after arriving in the country. The quarantine and contact tracing are part of Somalia's efforts to monitor and respond to any possible Ebola cases.\n\nThe decision follows growing concern about the Ebola outbreak in the DRC, which has been ongoing since earlier this year. The DRC has experienced multiple Ebola outbreaks in recent years, and neighboring countries have been on high alert. Uganda, which the returnees transited, has also been monitoring the situation closely. Somalia's health ministry has been working to strengthen its preparedness and response capabilities, including screening at points of entry and maintaining isolation facilities.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development is particularly significant. Many Somalis travel frequently between Somalia and other African countries for business, family, and other reasons. The quarantine of these individuals highlights the importance of vigilance and adherence to health guidelines when traveling. It also underscores the need for timely information and cooperation with health authorities to ensure the safety of communities in Somalia and abroad.\n\nThe ministry has not reported any confirmed cases of Ebola in Somalia so far, and the quarantine is a preventive measure. Health officials continue to urge the public to remain calm and follow official updates. The situation is being monitored closely, and further information will be provided as it becomes available.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/13/soomaaliya-ooo-karantiishay-10-qof-o-ka-soo-laabtay-dr-congo/",
